 -- jjbrucker <jjbrucker@foopgp.org>  Mon, 29 Jun 2026 18:14:45 +0200

onak-foopgp (0.6.5+foopgp1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Renamed source and binary package from onak to onak-foopgp; this
    fork ships ahead of vanilla onak 0.6.5 with five extra patches
    maintained against upstream pull requests. Once those land
    upstream this package will be retired in favour of plain onak.
  * Conflicts/Replaces/Provides onak so an upgrade from the Debian
    onak package is straightforward.
  * Maintainer transferred to the fork's owner; Jonathan McDowell
    remains the upstream author and Debian onak maintainer.
  * cleankey: cap UIDs and UATs per key at import (PR #6 upstream,
    merged 2026-06-28).
  * onak: add aged / dump-aged / clean-aged subcommands (PR #7).
  * merge, cleankey: collapse signatures per (version, sigtype,
    issuer) (PR #8).
  * cleankey: drop v3 keys unconditionally, retire the drop_v3
    toggle.
  * cleankey: add max_sigs_per_uid / max_sigs_per_uat caps.
  * template: introduce a minimal Mustache-style HTML/text engine
    that lets the CGI lookup pages be rendered from a template
    directory under /usr/share/onak/templates/ rather than from
    printf calls inside keyindex.c; adds a new template_dir
    setting in onak.ini.
  * keyindex: render op=index / op=vindex through templates. The
    vanilla template reproduces the legacy output byte-for-byte.
  * templates: ship the foopgp 2-column layout with client-side
    i18n. The onak-foopgp package wires template_dir at install
    time to /usr/share/onak/templates/foopgp so a fresh install
    serves the new identity-first rendering immediately.
  * debian/onak.{service,socket,...} renamed to onak-foopgp.{...};
    administrators must re-enable the unit after upgrade:
      systemctl enable --now onak-foopgp.socket

